From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] libalpm: avoid duplicating prefix when SYSHOOKDIR already
 starts with rootdir

`SYSHOOKDIR` is normally a system-relative path like "/usr/share/libalpm/
hooks/", and `alpm_initialize` concatenates `root + SYSHOOKDIR[1:]` to
get the hook dir under `root`. That works for the common Linux install
where root="/" and SYSHOOKDIR is genuinely relative.

When pacman is built with `--prefix=<non-system-dir>` (e.g.
`/i/pspdev-win/install` for our PSP toolchain), the meson DATAROOTDIR
that feeds SYSHOOKDIR bakes in the FULL prefix:

    #define SYSHOOKDIR "/i/pspdev-win/install/share/libalpm/hooks/"

`psp-pacman`'s wrapper script then runs pacman with `--root "${PSPDEV}"`,
so `myhandle->root` is also `/i/pspdev-win/install/`. The concat then
produces `<prefix>/<prefix>/share/libalpm/hooks/`, a bogus duplicated
path that `pacman -Sv` reports under "Hook Dirs".

This patch detects the case where SYSHOOKDIR already starts with root
and uses SYSHOOKDIR directly. For the normal Linux install (root="/"),
strncmp also matches and SYSHOOKDIR alone equals what the concat would
have produced, so this is a no-op.
---
 lib/libalpm/alpm.c | 18 ++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/libalpm/alpm.c b/lib/libalpm/alpm.c
--- a/lib/libalpm/alpm.c
+++ b/lib/libalpm/alpm.c
@@ -51,11 +51,20 @@ alpm_handle_t SYMEXPORT *alpm_initialize(const char *root, const char *dbpath,
 		goto cleanup;
 	}
 
-	/* to concatenate myhandle->root (ends with a slash) with SYSHOOKDIR (starts
-	 * with a slash) correctly, we skip SYSHOOKDIR[0]; the regular +1 therefore
-	 * disappears from the allocation */
-	MALLOC(hookdir, strlen(myhandle->root) + strlen(SYSHOOKDIR), goto nomem);
-	sprintf(hookdir, "%s%s", myhandle->root, &SYSHOOKDIR[1]);
+	/* SYSHOOKDIR is normally a system-relative path like
+	 * "/usr/share/libalpm/hooks/" and we concatenate it onto
+	 * myhandle->root. But when pacman is built with --prefix=<non-system-
+	 * dir>, meson bakes the full prefix into SYSHOOKDIR, and our wrapper
+	 * may pass the same prefix as --root; a naive concat would then double
+	 * the prefix. Detect that case and use SYSHOOKDIR as-is. For the
+	 * normal install (root="/") strncmp also matches and SYSHOOKDIR alone
+	 * equals what the concat would have produced. */
+	if(strncmp(myhandle->root, SYSHOOKDIR, strlen(myhandle->root)) == 0) {
+		STRDUP(hookdir, SYSHOOKDIR, goto nomem);
+	} else {
+		MALLOC(hookdir, strlen(myhandle->root) + strlen(SYSHOOKDIR), goto nomem);
+		sprintf(hookdir, "%s%s", myhandle->root, &SYSHOOKDIR[1]);
+	}
 	myhandle->hookdirs = alpm_list_add(NULL, hookdir);
 
 	/* set default database extension */
